From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:42:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: reset the buffer size before the ACPI Optimus caps
 call

_acpiCacheMethodData() passes the size the JT caps call left in rtnSize to the
NVOP caps call. After an empty JT reply the NVOP call fails for lack of space,
and after an oversized one a reply of that size could overwrite what follows the
4-byte optimusCaps. The result is passed on to GSP.

Set the size for the buffer that is actually passed.

Builds against 7.3 and boots; the failure path hasn't been run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/acpi_common.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/acpi_common.c b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/acpi_common.c
index 7bd8c52e..455354d5 100644
--- a/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/acpi_common.c
+++ b/src/nvidia/src/kernel/platform/acpi_common.c
@@ -1175,6 +1175,7 @@ _acpiCacheMethodData
     }
 
     // Fill in the Optimus caps Method Data.
+    rtnSize = sizeof(pGpu->acpiMethodData.capsMethodData.optimusCaps);
     status = osCallACPI_DSM(pGpu, ACPI_DSM_FUNCTION_NVOP, NVOP_FUNC_OPTIMUSCAPS,
                             &pGpu->acpiMethodData.capsMethodData.optimusCaps, &rtnSize);
     pGpu->acpiMethodData.capsMethodData.status = status;
